adjudication.rationale:
The diff adds `apps/web/pages/api/webhook/app-credential.ts` with a webhook secret check:

```ts
if (req.headers[process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_HEADER_NAME || "calcom-webhook-secret"] !== process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET) {
  return res.status(403)
}
```

If `CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET` is not configured (i.e., `process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET` is `undefined`) and the request omits the header (so `req.headers[...]` is also `undefined`), then the condition becomes `undefined !== undefined` which is `false`, so the request is accepted. Past that, the handler decrypts/parses attacker-controlled `keys` and will create/update a credential for arbitrary `userId` + `appSlug` (it only checks that the user and app exist), so this is a real fail-open authentication bug when sharing is enabled but the secret is forgotten/misconfigured. The recommendation to assert the secret is set is directly applicable; timing-safe comparison is an additional hardening suggestion.
